Welcome to the world of 'mini.pick' :)

So far, there is only one thing missing for me. Coming from Telescope (which I also love), I could use <M-h> and <M-l> from mini.move to move my cursor.

Judging by your dotfiles, I would take a guess that you indeed mean <M-h> to <M-l> to move cursor left and right. This comes from 'mini.basics' config.mappings.move_with_alt which you indeed enable. This is not the same as 'mini.move' which uses those keys by default in Normal and Visual modes (as opposed to just moving cursor in Insert, Command, and Terminal mode.
So with this in mind the answer: yes, you can customize which keys move cursor left and right. As 'mini.pick' implements its own picker life cycle with its special keys (and doesn't really have any real cursor active), you can override mappings.caret_left and mappings.caret_right.
In practice this will look something like this:
require('mini.pick').setup({
  mappings = {
    caret_left = '<M-h>',
    caret_right = '<M-l>',
  }
})
Note that this means that moving left and right with <Left> and <Right> keys will be overridden / disabled.
